'''Cyber Defender''' is an educational game on ''[[Minecraft Education]]''. It takes the form of a tower defense game with heavy influence from the theme of cyberattacks and protection from them, with most gameplay elements being symbolic of cybersecurity systems.<ref>https://education.minecraft.net/en-us/lessons/cyber-defender</ref>

== Summary ==
{{Expand section}}
This is similar to a tower defense game. [[Fox|Foxes]] and [[horses]] will pay the player at the marketplace while enemies will eat [[Sweet Berries|berries]] in the berry farm. Each enemy is designed after a different type of digital attack. To prevent enemies from eating the berry farm the player will have to place towers and gates. Friendly animals must also go through defenses; as such, too many defenses will also hurt friendly entities. If enemies reach the farm, the player will have to manually fight the enemies. Two maps exist: easier Forest, and harder Mesa.<ref>https://education.minecraft.net/en-us/blog/cyber-defender</ref>

=== Enemies ===
* {{EntityLink|Zoglin}}
* Disguised zoglin (ignored by skeleton towers)
* Fully disguised zoglin (ignored by skeleton towers, must be revealed by a blue gate)
* {{EntityLink|Spider}} (charges the player if it reaches the farm to earn back the player's points)
* [[Bee|Bees]] (appear in large swarms, representing Dedicated Denial of Service attacks)

=== Towers and Gates ===
Towers and gates help get rid of the zoglins.
* [[Skeleton]] tower (Antivirus)
* Orange gate (Basic firewall)
* Blue gate

